   "finding": "The unconditional failure-path preservation claim is unsupported: B is printed before _record_delivered. A failed B record write is swallowed without invalidating the prior A record. Returning to A in the same compaction generation can therefore match that old A tuple and suppress the required return persona.",
   "literal_claim": "Failed record read/write degrades toward redundant emission, not invented successful delivery.",
   "source_sequence": [
    "Persisted/session-matching tuple A,g exists.",
    "B is the actual effective mode and is printed by _inject_claude or _inject_codex.",
    "The atomic write for B fails before replacing the prior tuple; _record_delivered catches and passes.",
    "Effective mode returns to A,g; _already_delivered compares old tuple A,g and returns true, so no A emission follows B."
   ],
   "basis": "HW-01 explicitly requires actual A\u2192B\u2192A transitions. This is a source-confirmed failure path, not a runtime reproduction or original-host cause attribution.",
